{
  "version": "2026.10.04.1",
  "description": "What the TLS check offers a server, one probe each (FR-DET-04, decision D7): the protocol versions in 'protocols' and the weak cipher groups in 'cipher_groups'. A probe is a standard ClientHello; the scanner reads the server's first reply and closes, so no handshake completes. SSLv2 is not probed: it uses a different hello format and no current server speaks it. Suite codes and names are from the IANA TLS Cipher Suites registry (retrieved 2026-10-04); only RSA, DH, DHE, ECDH and ECDHE key exchanges are listed, because a web server does not use PSK, Kerberos or SRP suites. 'markers' recognise a group in the OpenSSL name of a negotiated suite (ssl.cipher()); the first group that matches wins, so the order is the order of severity. A group without 'suites' is recognised in a negotiated suite but not probed.",
  "source": {
    "registry": "IANA TLS Cipher Suites",
    "url": "https://www.iana.org/assignments/tls-parameters/tls-parameters.xhtml#tls-parameters-4",
    "retrieved": "2026-10-04"
  },
